  "body": "[https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#dom-media-playbackrate](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#dom-media-playbackrate)\r\n\r\nThis is what the current specification says about setting the `playbackRate` attribute: `Set playbackRate to the new value, and if the element is potentially playing, change the playback speed.`\r\n\r\nIf the element is **potentially playing** then all happens in the expected way: the `playbackRate` is updated and the playback speed of the media player is changed according to the new `playbackRate`. Now, if the element is **not potentially playing** then the change in the playback speed of the media player will never happen. The problem with allowing the `playbackRate` attribute change when the media element is not playing is that **we will be missing the change in the playback speed when the media starts playing**. In order to fix this, the playback speed of the media player needs to be updated according to the current `playbackRate` right before the media starts playing.",
